admitted to the psychiatric ward due to major
depression with psychotic features. She
refuses to take anything by mouth including
her medications because she believes that
she will die if she eats. Electroconvulsive
therapy (ECT) has been decided for her as a
life-saving measure and explained to her but
she refuses to consent to this treatment. She
is clinically stable for now. Which one of the
following is the next best step in her
management?','{"A":"Take consent from the Mental\nHealth Tribunal.","B":"Give ECT without consent under\nduty of care.","C":"Obtain consent from her husband.","D":"Give her nasogastric feeding and\nanti-depressants.","E":"Obtain consent from the hospital\nadministrator."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-a2d36fefc35d","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d8625f15afe1fdfc4804","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_page":142,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"bc245892b2f182af0c11","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":388,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"d8625f15afe1fdfc4804","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Ethics file 3.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":142,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Ethics/Population Health","stem":"A 52-year-old woman is involuntarily\nadmitted to the psychiatric ward due to major\ndepression with psychotic features. She\nrefuses to take anything by mouth including\nher medications because she believes that\nshe will die if she eats. Electroconvulsive\ntherapy (ECT) has been decided for her as a\nlife-saving measure and explained to her but\nshe refuses to consent to this treatment. She\nis clinically stable for now. Which one of the\nfollowing is the next best step in her\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"Take consent from the Mental\nHealth Tribunal.","B":"Give ECT without consent under\nduty of ca