department of the local hospital you are working
in after an episode of vomiting a large amount
of fresh blood. A couple of hours before the
presentation, he had binge drinking, which was
followed by retching several times and vomiting
before he vomited blood. This is the first time he
has had such a problem. He has enjoyed good
health otherwise and has no complaints except
indigestion after meals, for which he takes over-
the-counter antacids. He does not smoke but
drinks equivalent to 30 grams of alcohol every
day. Which of the following could be the most
