school. The breasts have not started budding
on examination, but pubic and axillary hair
growth is present. No abdominal mass,
tenderness, or rebound tenderness is noted
on examination. The remainder of the exam
is unremarkable. The patient refuses a
vaginal exam. Which one of the following can
