month history of secondary infertility. Her
first child, fathered by the same partner, was
born four years ago after she was conceived
spontaneously and through an uneventful
vaginal delivery. She has always had irregular
periods occurring every 2 to 4 months. On
examination, she is obese (BMI>32) and
otherwise normal. Ultrasonography of the
pelvis reveals 12 small cysts of 3-6 mm in
diameter in the left and 20 cysts of about the
Same size in the right ovary. A sperm analysis
of the partner is normal. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate next step in
management?','{"A":"Metformin.","B":"Clomiphene citrate.","C":"Ovulation induction with\ngonadotropins.","D":"Laparoscopic ovarian drilling.","E":"In-vitro fertilization. ©"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-893237926976","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b2b98e09eb9e1361e045","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_page":57,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"b2b98e09eb9e1361e045","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":57,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Gynaecology","stem":"A 30-year-old woman presents with a 12-\nmonth history of secondary infertility. Her\nfirst child, fathered by the same partner, was\nborn four years ago after she was conceived\nspontaneously and through an uneventful\nvaginal delivery. She has always had irregular\nperiods occurring every 2 to 4 months. On\nexamination, she is obese (BMI>32) and\notherwise normal. Ultrasonography of the\npelvis reveals 12 small cysts of 3-6 mm in\ndiameter in the left and 20 cysts of about the\nSame size in the right ovary. A sperm analysis\nof the partner is normal. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most appropriate next step in\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"Metformin.","B":"Clomiphene citrate.","C":"Ovulation induction with\ngonadotropins.","D":"Laparoscopic ovarian drilling.","E":"In-vitro fertilization. ©"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer"