irregular periods every 2 to 3 months lasting
7-10 days for the past seven years. She
undergoes a diagnostic dilation and curettage
(D&C) in the premenstrual period. Which one
of the following findings on histological
examinations, if present, is the most likely
cause of her problem?','{"A":"Normal secretory endometrium.","B":"Cystic glandular hyperplasia.","C":"Atypical hyperplasia.","D":"An endometrial polyp.","E":"Endometrial cancer."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-6eb13877b3c7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"0f7c8dd1727020a0d511","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_page":72,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"21af5ec900d205e2993a","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_page":73,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"3d7dcf5d21ea82c2727b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1032,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"0f7c8dd1727020a0d511","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":72,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Gynaecology","stem":"A 49-year-old woman presents with heavy\nirregular periods every 2 to 3 months lasting\n7-10 days for the past seven years. She\nundergoes a diagnostic dilation and curettage\n(D&C) in the premenstrual period. Which one\nof the following findings on histological\nexaminations, if present, is the most likely\ncause of her problem?","options":{"A":"Normal secretory endometrium.","B":"Cystic glandular hyperplasia.","C":"Atypical hyperplasia.","D":"An endometrial polyp.","E":"Endomet