practice with a complaint of premenstrual
abdominal bloating, irritability, and
uneasiness for the past 6 months. These
symptoms begin 3-4 days before her
anticipated periods and ease off within 1 to 2
days of her menstrual flow. Recently, she had
to take a few days off work because of the
intensity of her symptoms. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate next step in
management?','{"A":"Relaxation therapy.","B":"Sertraline 50mg daily in the second\nhalf of anticipated luteal phase.","C":"Evening primrose oil.","D":"Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory\ndrugs (NSAIDs).","E":"Low-dose oral contraceptives (OCP)\nwith shortened pill-free intervals."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[20],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-15ff22703da8","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"65195d6177aa0428c119","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (2).pdf","source_page":20,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"65195d6177aa0428c119","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":20,"supporting_pages":[20],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Gynaecology","stem":"A 27-year-old woman presents to your\npractice with a complaint of premenstrual\nabdominal bloating, irritability, and\nuneasiness for the past 6 months. These\nsymptoms begin 3-4 days before her\nanticipated periods and ease off within 1 to 2\ndays of her menstrual flow. Recently, she had\nto take a few days off work because of the\nintensity of her symptoms. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most appropriate next step in\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"Relaxation therapy.","B":"Sertraline 50mg daily in the second\nhalf of anticipated luteal phase.","C":"Evening primrose oil.","D":"Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory\ndrugs (NSAIDs).","E":"Low-dose oral contraceptives (OCP)\nwith shortened pill-free intervals."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"sourc