contraception advice. Two years ago, while on
combined oral contraceptive pills (COCP), she
developed deep vein thrombosis; therefore, she
was switched to a progestogen-only pill (POP).
Last year, she came off the pill to start a family,
but her pregnancy turned out ectopic and
aborted six months ago. She wants to begin
contraception again as she is not planning any
pregnancies in the near future. Which of the
following would be the correct advice in this
regard?','{"A":"She cannot take POP.","B":"She can start taking POP.","C":"She can start taking COCP, but she\nwill need prophylactic\nanticoagulation.","D":"She can take POP after 12 months of\nher ectopic pregnancy.","E":"She can start taking COCP."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (3).pdf","supporting_pages":[22],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-d22fb20fc183","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"ab21afa8aa81267bc8ed","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (3).pdf","source_page":22,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"ab21afa8aa81267bc8ed","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (3).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":22,"supporting_pages":[22],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Gynaecology","stem":"Alison is 33 years old and has come to you for\ncontraception advice. Two years ago, while on\ncombined oral contraceptive pills (COCP), she\ndeveloped deep vein thrombosis; therefore, she\nwas switched to a progestogen-only pill (POP).\nLast year, she came off the pill to start a family,\nbut her pregnancy turned out ectopic and\naborted six months ago. She wants to begin\ncontraception again as she is not planning any\npregnancies in the near future. Which of the\nfollowing would be the correct advice in this\nregard?","options":{"A":"She cannot take POP.","B":"She can start taking POP.","C":"She can start taking COCP, but she\nwill need prophylactic\nanticoagulation.","D":"She can take POP after 12 months of\nher ectopic pregnancy.","E":"She can start taking COCP."},"source_answer":nu